 "category": "comic",
 "summary": "Book-style viewer for Windows that treats folders and archives as books and images as pages. Very configurable: every action is a command with its own keys, mouse gestures and scripts, plus bookshelf, bookmarks, playlists and two-page manga spreads. Videos play through Windows or an installed VLC.",
 "where_it_wins": [
  "Extremely deep customisation: commands, gestures, JavaScript scripting",
  "Two-page spread with right-to-left reading and page splitting",
  "Nested archives and archive passwords (via 7z.dll)",
  "Saved playlists, history and search with date/size/regex operators",
  "Image effects panel, printing, export as ZIP/folder",
  "Microsoft Store and portable ZIP builds"
 ],
 "where_schnellbild_wins": [
  "Runs natively on the Mac (NeeView is Windows only)",
  "Videos (MKV, WebM, AVI) play out of the box without installing VLC",
  "Photos and videos together in one thumbnail grid with folder previews",
  "Dual pane with F5/F6, undo of renames, moves and trash",
  "App Sandbox, no network, notarized and attested builds",
  "20 interface languages"
 ],
